America's greatest hero Kyle joined  street fighter 5 in the next update and  ahead of his release we got to spend a  little time sonic booming and flash  kicking with him first off it's worth  saying that is probably the least  changed character overall while everyone  has had their inputs and styles fiddled  with to make them more distinct guy all  feels largely the same he's the game's  first fully charged character with no  quarter half or whole circle motion  inputs so if you played him in three  fire four he'll be very comfortable with  him from the outset overall he's a  little more open to being played as an  aggressive offense character but he's  still also a defensive wall kyle has all  his unique normal attacks and they do  pretty much the same thing as they did  in Street fire for his back fist is a  great way to catch people off-guard if  you cover it with a sonic boom his hop  kick can be steered towards or away from  opponents to keep the pressure on while  moving his forward knee is a super fast  way of getting in and his  gravity-defying upside-down kick will  punish sweeps on top of all that he's  got a few target combos to use as  extenders and as an easy way to get  damaged after a crush counter  these V scale is excellent at  controlling space and getting the  opponent where you want them press the  two medium attack buttons and he'll  leave a small sonic boom directly in  front of them which is handy for keeping  people of you however if you charge your  sonic boom as you're using your V skill  and then execute at the moment the V  skill is out you can send both hurtling  towards the enemy the projectile version  is very quick and gives the sonic boom  two hits of damage or durability  together they make guys viable game very  strong activate geils V skill which is  called solid puncher and you get some  sweet yellow rave wristbands on top of  that you can do a sonic boom and spam  the other punch bonds to follow up with  additional sonic booms the speed at  which these travel depend on the punch  by on your pressing with the hard as the  fastest and light as a slowest you can  vary these up to exert control over the  battlefield and dissuade your opponent  from jumping over them a maximum of five  of these sonic booms can be on the  screen at the same time and the initial  sonic boom can be executed instantly by  pressing the two heart attack buttons at  the same time instead of using the  chargeback forward motion this is really  good for extending combos and dishing  out big damage in a pinch  the flash kicks as always a very good  range and priority it's worth knowing  that only the e x versions have  invincibility so if you have a habit of  recovering from a knockdown with a flash  kick it will get nullified by throws and  vault I'm normals guy also has two  versions of his critical art in his  normal mode sonic hurricane is great for  dishing out big war damage punishing bad  fireballs comboing and chipping if V  trigger is activated however it becomes  sonic tempest although these moves look  the same it has a greater range and  damage since activating v-trigger stops  time you can use this brief window to  charge up a tempest and land it when  time resumes one big change the goal is  that by holding down and forward he does  a crouch walk this is really slow but  allows you to advance while maintaining  the charge you need to flash kick once  girl is in the hands of more players we  imagine a lot of experimentation will be  done with this to come up with good ways  to set up flash kicks overall girl feels  familiar but has a bunch of really  strong tools it might be too early to  tell but right now he seems like he's  going to be in the upper tail of  characters he's got all the right tools  about her ass the opponent exploit the  mistakes and his own the eager players  he's going to be sending a lot of people  home to be a family man
 

